and use, with no account and no paywall. If it earns a place on your Mac, you can buy me a coffee. The app stays free either way.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Does my Mac need a notch?</summary><p>Otto is designed around the notch, but you can choose a floating panel in setup or in Settings. It opens with a shortcut instead. Otto needs macOS 13 or later.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Which calendars does it read?</summary><p>The ones in your Mac\u2019s Calendar app, including iCloud, Google and Exchange accounts you\u2019ve added there. Otto only reads events. It never creates, edits or deletes one.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Where is my data?</summary><p>On your Mac. To-dos and notes are stored locally, and a Markdown copy lives in a folder you choose (by default Documents/Otto). There is no Otto account and nothing syncs through a server.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>What does the anonymous usage data include?</summary><p>Only if you say yes during setup: which features are used, the app and macOS version, and a random ID that isn\u2019t linked to you. Never your to-dos, notes, calendar or anything you type. You can see exactly what is sent in Settings. <a href=\"privacy.html\" style=\"color:var(--lilac)\">Full details</a>.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Will macOS warn me when I open it?</summary><p>No. Otto is signed with a Developer ID and notarized by Apple, so it opens like any other app. It also updates itself from inside the app.</p></details>\n      <details><summary>Which languages does it speak?</summary><p>English and Italian.</p></details>", "LOG": "<div class=\"entry\"><time datetime=\"2026-10-03\">3 October 2026</time><div><h3>Join and snooze from the alert</h3><p>Press \u2318\u21b5 to join and S to snooze while a meeting alert is up. Alerts are no longer skipped after you close the notch on an open note.</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"entry\"><time datetime=\"2026-10-01\">1 October 2026</time><div><h3>A new Settings window</h3><p>Nine pages with search and native macOS controls. Pick your layout, theme and opening speed in one place.</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"entry\"><time datetime=\"2026-09-29\">29 September 2026</time><div><h3>The logo looks around</h3><p>During setup, the two O\u2019s in Otto\u2019s logo now look around and blink. They stay still if you use Reduce Motion.</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"entry\"><time datetime=\"2026-09-26\">26 September 2026</time><div><h3>A friendlier first run, and sleepy lists</h3><p>A new setup guides you through tasks, notes and meetings. Empty lists now take a nap instead of saying nothing.</p></div></div>\n", "APPLE": "<svg class=\"apple\" viewBox=\"0 0 814 1000\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M788.1 340.9c-5.8 4.5-108.2 62.2-108.2 190.5 0 148.4 130.3 200.9 134.2 202.2-.6 3.2-20.7 71.9-68.7 141.9-42.8 61.6-87.5 123.1-155.5 123.1s-85.5-39.5-164-39.5c-76.5 0-103.7 40.8-165.9 40.8s-105.6-57-155.5-127C46.7 790.7 0 663 0 541.8c0-194.4 126.4-297.5 250.8-297.5 66.1 0 121.2 43.4 162.7 43.4 39.5 0 101.1-46 176.3-46 28.5 0 130.9 2.6 198.3 99.2zm-234-181.5c31.1-36.9 53.1-88.1 53.1-139.3 0-7.1-.6-14.3-1.9-20.1-50.6 1.9-110.8 33.7-147.1 75.8-28.5 32.4-55.1 83.6-55.1 135.5 0 7.8 1.3 15.6 1.9 18.1 3.2.6 8.4 1.3 13.6 1.3 45.4 0 102.5-30.4 135.5-71.3z\"/></svg>", "LOGO": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 883 430\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-label=\"Otto\"><path d=\"M605.409 147.083V74.2884C605.409 70.2867 602.135 67.0126 598.134 67.0126H560.448C556.447 67.0126 553.173 63.7385 553.173 59.7368V7.27825C553.173 3.27655 549.899 0.00244141 545.898 0.00244141H468.234C464.233 0.00244141 460.959 3.27655 460.959 7.27825V59.7368C460.959 63.7385 457.685 67.0126 453.683 67.0126H408.177C404.175 67.0126 400.901 63.7385 400.901 59.7368V7.27825C400.901 3.27655 397.627 0.00244141 393.626 0.00244141H315.962C311.961 0.00244141 308.687 3.27655 308.687 7.27825V59.7368C308.687 63.7385 305.413 67.0126 301.412 67.0126H281.732C277.731 67.0126 274.457 70.2